      "id": "https://www.cotidianulagricol.ro/anfa-si-bayer-lanseaza-o-initiativa-de-formare-dedicata-femeilor-din-agricultura-in-cadrul-evenimentului-femei-care-hranesc-romania/",
      "url": "https://www.cotidianulagricol.ro/anfa-si-bayer-lanseaza-o-initiativa-de-formare-dedicata-femeilor-din-agricultura-in-cadrul-evenimentului-femei-care-hranesc-romania/",
      "title": "[cotidianulagricol.ro] Agriculture groups launch training and scholarships to build farm workforce",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.cotidianulagricol.ro&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nAgricultural organizations in North America, Europe and South Korea announced new training, career-education and scholarship programs aimed at developing farm skills and helping people enter agricultural work. In Romania, the National Association of Women in Agriculture and Bayer launched a program of leadership, communication and technical workshops for women, set to begin in 2027. In Saskatchewan, Agriculture in the Classroom began a fundraising campaign with a matching pledge of up to $35,000.\n\nOther initiatives include a free AgCareers.com classroom kit for middle- and high-school students, a Montana FFA event seeking partners for more than 2,000 students, and a new North Dakota conference on farm communication and business planning. South Korea’s Daesan Rural Foundation is accepting applications for five scholarships that cover tuition for up to four semesters. Application deadlines include Nov. 2 for women involved in Ontario beef operations seeking conference support and Nov. 11 for the South Korean scholarships.",
      "date_published": "2026-10-22T01:18:00+00:00",
